 // Called before quitting to leave a net game
 // without hanging the other players
 //
+// JERKWAD: leave the netgame NOW. Exported so the page can call it when the
+// tab is closing (pagehide): the server tells its clients the game is over,
+// a client tells the server it is going. Nothing here waits or sleeps, so it
+// is safe from an unload handler and from the fatal-error path — the stock
+// NET_SV_Shutdown/NET_CL_Disconnect pair each sleep-wait up to five seconds
+// for acknowledgements, which under ASYNCIFY means unwinding the stack from
+// inside exit(), and that is how one fatal error used to turn into thousands.
+EMSCRIPTEN_KEEPALIVE void jw_net_leave(void)
+{
+    NET_SV_LeaveNow();
+    NET_CL_LeaveNow();
+}
